    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-professor-department-of-physical-therapy-12-mo-tt-birmingham-alabama-12507": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Department of Physical Therapy (12 Mo, TT)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Department of Physical Therapy (12 Mo, TT) in Birmingham, Alabama | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant Professor, Department of Physical Therapy (12 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Share Save Job Apply for This Job ASSISTANT PROFESSOR DEPARTMENT OF PHYSICAL THERAPY (Tenure Track, 12-month) July 16, 2026 REVISED: To extend application deadline from August 15, 2026 to September 11, 2026. Samford University’s School of Health Professions seeks a collaborative faculty member interested in serving in a Christian university environment to apply for the position of Assistant Professor in the Department of Physical Therapy. This full-time, tenure-track faculty position is a 12-month appointment and will begin October 1, 2026 . Qualifications: Qualified candidates will be a graduate of a CAPTE-accredited physical therapy program and have a minimum of three years of experience as a practicing physical therapist by start date. In addition, candidates must hold an academic doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, DSc or similar) or be actively enrolled in an academic doctoral program by the start date in order to meet CAPTE Standards and Required Elements for Accreditation Standard 4 (Updated Sept. 16, 2025). Additional requirements include: •\tEligibility for licensure as a Physical Therapist in Alabama •\tA commitment to academic excellence •\tAbility to work effectively with faculty, students and colleagues •\tWillingness to engage in community outreach activities, including serving in our pro-bono physical therapy clinic. •\tWillingness to support the Christian mission of Samford University and the College of Health Sciences •\tWillingness to travel for university-related purposes, as needed Responsibilities: Major responsibilities of the position include but are not limited to: •\tTeach courses in the DPT curriculum •\tMentor students •\tEngage in scholarly activity, including research, presentations, and publications •\tEngage in departmental, school, college, and/or university service as assigned •\tParticipate in departmental initiatives, program assessment, and accreditation activities •\tSupport curriculum development and continuous improvement •\tFoster a collaborative and inclusive environment for students, faculty, and staff •\tOther responsibilities assigned by department chair, dean, provost, or president and those described in the Samford University Faculty Handbook sections A6.1 and A6.2. Preference will be given to candidates with the following qualifications: •\tExperience teaching in a CAPTE-accredited PT program The College of Health Sciences includes four schools: School of Health Professions, Moffett & Sanders School of Nursing, McWhorter School of Pharmacy, and School of Public Health. The College offers multiple degree programs and majors within the health sciences with an inter-professional education focus that reflects today’s team approach to health care delivery and professional practice. Located in the Homewood suburb of Birmingham, Alabama, Samford ( samford.edu ) is a leading Christian university offering undergraduate programs grounded in the liberal arts with an array of nationally recognized graduate and professional schools. Founded in 1841, Samford enrolls 6,324 students from 44 states, Puerto Rico and 16 countries in its 10 academic schools with 450 full-time faculty. Samford is ranked #3 in the nation for career preparation and #7 in the nation for student learning opportunities as listed in The Wall Street Journal (2026). The University is dedicated to the promotion of rigorous academic inquiry in a Christian setting. The University seeks and prefers employee applicants of the Christian faith and offers competitive salaries with a generous benefits package. Application: Applications will be accepted until September 11, 2026 . Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vita, the names of three professional references, Application for Faculty Position and Faculty Applicant Christian Mission Statement. The successful candidate must pass a background check, and applicants must be authorized to work in the United States, as Samford will not sponsor any employment visas for this position. “Application for Faculty Position” can be found at: https://www.samford.edu/departments/files/Human_Resources/application-for-faculty-employment.pdf “Faculty Applicant Christian Mission Statement” can be found at: https://www.samford.edu/departments/files/academic-affairs/Faculty-Applicant-Christian-Mission-Statement.docx Please submit all materials in PDF format to: [email protected] ATTN: DPT- TT Asst Faculty Position In accordance with applicable federal and state laws, such as Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act, and the Americans with Disabilities Act and ADA Amendments, the University does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, color, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, religion, or any other protected status under federal, state or local law applicable to the University, in its education policies, programs, and activities, in its admissions policies, in employment policies and practices, and all other areas of the University. As a faith-based institution, the University is exempted from certain laws and regulations concerning discrimination. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Health Professions Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Program Director, MS Occupational Therapy Columbia International University Columbia, South Carolina Posted - September 8, 2026 View Civil Engineering Faculty Northwestern College ORANGE CITY, Iowa Posted - September 9, 2026 View Computer Science Faculty Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Posted - September 9, 2026 View Adjunct Faculty – College Math for Elementary Teaching Moody Bible Institute Chicago, Illinois Posted - September 8, 2026 View Mathematics & Statistics Faculty Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Posted - September 9, 2026 View Assistant Professor of Children and Family Ministry Moody Bible Institute Chicago, Illinois Posted - September 8, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations Ohio West Palm Beach, Florida St. Paul, Minnesota Alabama ORANGE CITY, Iowa Houston, Texas Iowa Minnesota Virginia Texas Virginia Beach, Virginia Portland, Oregon Cedarville, Ohio Azusa, California Florida Oregon California Birmingham, Alabama Michigan Longview, Texas Grand Rapids, Michigan Trending Companies Azusa Pacific University Houston Christian University Calvin University Cedarville University Samford University Northwestern College Regent University Palm Beach Atlantic University LeTourneau University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Education Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Religion Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Computer science Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
