    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/nursing-assistant-professor-holland-michigan-12615": {
      "title": "Nursing - Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Nursing - Assistant Professor in Holland, Michigan | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Nursing - Assistant Professor Hope College Holland, Michigan Share Save Job Apply for This Job Position Title Nursing - Assistant Professor Classification Title Faculty Full Time (.75-1.0 FTE) Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligibility Department Nursing Job Description Hope College invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in the Department of Nursing. The successful candidate will primarily teach undergraduate nursing courses in nursing research, adult health (medical-surgical) nursing, and other BSN courses as assigned. Teaching responsibilities may include classroom, laboratory, clinical, and practicum instruction. Responsibilities include: Developing and delivering high-quality instruction; Designing, administering, and evaluating student learning experiences and assessments; Supervising students in clinical and practicum settings; Advising and mentoring students academically and professionally; Contributing to curriculum development, program assessment, and continuous quality improvement. Faculty are expected to maintain an active program of scholarship, engage in ongoing professional development, and provide service to the department, college, and profession consistent with the expectations of a tenure-track appointment at Hope College. Is this a visiting faculty position? No Rank Assistant Qualifications Required Qualifications Current or eligible for registered nurse licensure in the State of Michigan. Demonstrated expertise in adult health (medical-surgical) nursing. Evidence of effective teaching or clinical education. Strong communication, collaboration, and mentoring skills. Earned PhD in Nursing or a closely related nursing terminal degree by the time of appointment. Candidates who are All But Dissertation (ABD) and are expected to complete the doctoral degree by the date of appointment or within one year of hire are encouraged to apply. Successful applicants will demonstrate a commitment to all aspects of Hope’s mission as a liberal arts college. Hope College is grounded in robust ecumenical Christian aspirations and strives for inclusive excellence. As part of the application, we ask all candidates to describe how they will engage with and support the holistic mission of the College, particularly how their Christian faith, commitment to the liberal arts, and inclusive excellence shape their work as teachers, scholars, and mentors. More guidelines for Hope College candidate’s response to the mission statement can be found at hope.edu/jobs . Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching undergraduate nursing research, evidence-based practice, and adult health (medical-surgical) nursing. Experience supervising undergraduate research, evidence-based practice, or capstone/practicum projects. Demonstrated record of scholarly activity with the potential to establish and sustain a program of scholarship consistent with tenure expectations. Commitment to student-centered teaching and mentoring within a liberal arts environment. Physical Demands This position requires remaining in a sitting or standing position for frequent periods of time; uses office machinery such as a computers, printers, copy machines; Occasionally involves moving items over 10 pounds; frequently will move between different offices/workspaces/buildings; and requires effective communication abilities. In the case of temporary or permanent condition(s) that require(s) accommodation(s), reasonable accommodation(s) may be requested. Pre-employment Screenings “All offers of employment are contingent upon a background check. Some positions may have position specific requirements, such as education/licensure/certification verification, a physical, drug screening, credit checks and/or transportation record review.” Posting Detail Information Posting Number 2026-004FR Job Posting Open Date 08/04/2026 Job Posting Close Date 09/20/2026 Open Until Filled No Is this position available for sponsorship No Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://jobs.hope.edu/postings/5512 Job Information Job Category: Nurse Education: Doctorate Degree Experience: 5 - 10 years Related Jobs Assistant/Associate Professor of History LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 3, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing, Undergraduate Program - Community Nursing Palm Beach Atlantic University West Palm Beach, Florida Posted - August 21, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing, Undergraduate Program - Pediatrics Palm Beach Atlantic University West Palm Beach, Florida Posted - August 21, 2026 View Director, The Center for Academic MInistry LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - August 21, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing Crown College Saint Bonifacius, Minnesota Posted - September 1, 2026 View Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - August 21, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Alabama Oregon Cedarville, Ohio Minnesota Ohio Longview, Texas Houston, Texas Azusa, California Birmingham, Alabama Texas Portland, Oregon ORANGE CITY, Iowa St. Paul, Minnesota Virginia Beach, Virginia California West Palm Beach, Florida Iowa Virginia Florida Trending Companies Azusa Pacific University Regent University Palm Beach Atlantic University Houston Christian University Samford University LeTourneau University Cedarville University Northwestern College Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Education Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
