    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-associate-professor-of-history-longview-texas-12613": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of History",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of History in Longview, Texas | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant/Associate Professor of History LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Share Save Job Apply for This Job Commute Time Show on map From Location To Location 2100 S Mobberly Ave, Longview, TX 75602, USA LeTourneau University, a vibrant and growing interdenominational, evangelical Christian university, known for high-quality STEM programs that attract students of outstanding academic ability, invites applications and nominations for the position of Assistant/Associate Professor of History, Department of Humanities & Social Sciences.  This is a tenure-track position, with rank negotiable based on experience.  This faculty member will play a central role in leading and developing the University’s History major while also engaging students across a wide array of science & technical disciplines. This individual will spearhead efforts to integrate historical knowledge with communication and analytical skill development for students majoring in fields such as engineering, aviation, and computer science. This is a nine-month position with the possibility of summer teaching. Classes and other responsibilities are conducted primarily on weekdays but could include some evening classes and independent studies.  Attendance is required at some evening and weekend events. RESPONSIBILITIES: •\tTeach a full-time load of courses in History, including preparation of course materials and assessments. •\tTeach a wide variety of courses across the curriculum from freshman to senior level with a four course (12 hour) load per Fall and Spring semester typically consisting of three lower-level and one upper-level course per semester. •\tOffer engaging introductory courses that build foundational historical knowledge and essential communication and analytical skills. •\tTeach a range of courses that may include, depending on expertise and program needs, foundational survey courses in US and Western history. •\tDevelop upper-level courses that deepen students’ understanding of historical themes and align with their academic and vocational interests. •\tProvide strategic leadership in re-envisioning the role of the humanities within a Christian Polytechnic context. •\tParticipate actively in the university learning community by serving on department, school, and/or university committees and special service assignments. •\tParticipate in student advising, success, and retention programs. •\tCommitment to academic scholarship in the field of expertise. QUALIFICATIONS: •\tLeTourneau University seeks an individual with an enthusiastic and contagious Christian faith who is committed to teaching, research, and leadership at a small, dynamic Christian University where the integration of faith and academic excellence is paramount. The candidate must be in genuine agreement with the University’s Statement of Faith and Community Covenant for life and work at LeTourneau. •\tAn earned doctorate (Ph.D.) in History, from an accredited university or in a closely related field. Candidates who are ABD with an estimated conferral date before May 2028 may be considered. •\tPreferred specialization in U.S. History, though strong candidates in related fields will be considered. •\tDemonstrated teaching competency •\tInterpersonal skills to effectively and professionally interact with students, colleagues, and administrators in a university learning community •\tThe successful candidate will be able to think creatively and critically about the essential role of the humanities (and writing, in particular) within the “Christian Polytechnic University” mission and provide leadership for efforts to fully infuse the humanities within the learning environment and campus culture of LeTourneau University. This includes developing communication and analytical skills in students majoring in technical fields such as engineering, aviation, computer science, etc. SALARY AND BENEFITS: The salary is competitive and commensurate with experience and other qualifications. LeTourneau University provides a significant benefit package, which includes medical and life insurance and contribution to a retirement program. DATE POSITION IS AVAILABLE: Fall 2027 PROCEDURE FOR APPLICATION OR NOMINATION: Interested applicants should submit a letter of interest, CV, list of references, copies of unofficial transcripts, and answers to several faith questions available in the online application form on the university’s website linked below. The review process will begin October 15th, 2026, and all applications received by October 30th, 2026, will receive full consideration. Applications after that date will be reviewed as received until the position is filled. To apply, visit www.letu.edu/jobs-faculty. Questions about the search process may be directed to [email protected] . In accordance with applicable provisions of federal law, applicants for employment who are in agreement with the educational mission of LeTourneau University and applicants for admission to educational programs or activities are considered without discrimination on the basis of race, age, sex, handicapping condition, national origin or genetic information.  Inquiries about this policy should be directed to the Director of Human Resources, (903) 233-4170. ABOUT LETOURNEAU UNIVERSITY: LeTourneau University is known as “the Christian Polytechnic University,” a comprehensive yet STEM-focused, evangelical, and interdenominational Christian institution. LeTourneau is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges and is a member of the Council for Christian Colleges and Universities. LeTourneau offers more than 140 graduate and undergraduate courses of study in aviation, engineering, education, business, psychology and counseling, arts and sciences, nursing, and theology. Students enjoy the opportunity to take classes in person, online, or in a dual credit format. Approximately 3,000 students attend LeTourneau University, including in-person, online, and dual credit students. With the average class size of 16 and a 13-to-1 student to faculty ratio, students are able to develop close relationships with world-class faculty. Professors are experts in their chosen field, credentialed with degrees from the top universities around the world. Many come to LeTourneau straight from industry or missions contexts, offering real-world experiences in the classroom and rich mentoring relationships with students. At LeTourneau, students receive both academic excellence and intentional spiritual formation because the integration of faith and learning is paramount to the educational mission of the university. Faculty and staff are active in students’ lives and encourage students to know Jesus Christ and the abundant life He offers. LeTourneau consistently ranks among the top colleges and universities in the nation and the state of Texas: Top National Tier, Best Regional University in the Western Region and Best Undergraduate Engineering Program (U.S. News & World Report); Best Small Colleges in America, Most Conservative College in Texas, Best Christian College in Texas (Niche.com) in 2022. Also, LeTourneau ranks in the top 20 Best Value Colleges in Texas (Payscale.com) and Best Value Schools (U.S. News & World Report). LeTourneau University was founded in 1946 by businessman and devout Christian, R.G. LeTourneau, and his wife, Evelyn. Its beautiful, 162-acre, residential campus is located in Longview, TX. Learn more at www.letu.edu. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - History Education: Doctorate Degree Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - August 21, 2026 View Virginia and Tom Williams Endowed Chair of American Literature, Department of English, Associate Professor or Professor Baylor University Waco, Texas Posted - July 15, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Finance Grace College & Seminary Winona Lake, Indiana Posted - April 29, 2026 View Associate Professor of Communication Regent University Virginia Beach, Virginia Posted - August 28, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Cybersecurity Azusa Pacific University Azusa, California Posted - August 27, 2026 View Program Director, MS Occupational Therapy Columbia International University Columbia, South Carolina Posted - September 8, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations Iowa ORANGE CITY, Iowa Azusa, California Cedarville, Ohio St. Paul, Minnesota Virginia Ohio Longview, Texas Minnesota Houston, Texas Texas California West Palm Beach, Florida Oregon Alabama Florida Birmingham, Alabama Portland, Oregon Virginia Beach, Virginia Trending Companies Cedarville University Houston Christian University Azusa Pacific University Regent University Palm Beach Atlantic University Northwestern College Samford University LeTourneau University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Health Professions Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Engineering Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Education Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
