    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-professor-department-of-communication-and-media-9-mo-tt-birmingham-alabama-12611": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Department of Communication and Media (9 Mo, TT)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Department of Communication and Media (9 Mo, TT) in Birmingham, Alabama | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant Professor, Department of Communication and Media (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Share Save Job Apply for This Job Assistant Professor Department of Communication and Media (9-month appointment, Tenure Track) September 2, 2026 Samford University’s Howard College of Arts and Sciences invites individuals interested in serving in a Christian University environment to apply for an Assistant Professor position in the Department of Communication and Media. This full-time tenure track position is a 9-month appointment and carries a twenty-four (24) credit-hour teaching load. The position will begin in August 2027. Qualified candidates will hold a Ph.D. or be ABD, near completion, in communication studies or a closely related field from an institutionally accredited college or university (or equivalent). Candidates with the ability to teach courses in interpersonal communication, quantitative research methods, and organizational communication are preferred. Successful candidates should have an active research agenda and demonstrated excellence in teaching, with at least three years of college teaching at the undergraduate level. Candidates may also be asked to participate in Samford’s general education program. ABD candidates will be considered at the rank of Instructor, with commensurate salary, until Ph.D. is completed. The Department of Communication and Media is home to Samford’s award-winning student media and hosts an annual speaker forum (Robinson Forum - a lecture series in cooperation with The Washington Post). Located in the Homewood suburb of Birmingham, Alabama, Samford ( samford.edu ) is a leading Christian university offering undergraduate programs grounded in the liberal arts with an array of nationally recognized graduate and professional schools. Founded in 1841, Samford enrolls 6,324 students from 44 states, Puerto Rico and 16 countries in its 10 academic schools with 450 full-time faculty. Samford is ranked #3 in the nation for career preparation and #8 in the nation for student learning opportunities as listed in The Wall Street Journal (2026). The University is dedicated to the promotion of rigorous academic inquiry in a Christian setting. The University seeks and prefers employee applicants of the Christian faith and offers competitive salaries with a generous benefits package. Review of applications will begin October 2, 2026, and applications will continue to be accepted until October 16, 2026. Please submit (via email below in .pdf format), an application letter, curriculum vitae with names and contact information of three references, description of teaching experience and interests, description of research plans, along with an Application for Faculty Position and the Faculty Applicant Christian Mission Statement (links below). Salary is dependent upon qualifications and experience. The successful candidate must pass a background check. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States, as Samford will not sponsor any employment visas for this position. Application for Faculty Position can be found at: https://www.samford.edu/departments/files/Human_Resources/application-for-faculty-employment.pdf Faculty Applicant Christian Mission Statement can be found at: https://www.samford.edu/departments/files/academic-affairs/Faculty-Applicant-Christian-Mission-Statement.docx Please submit all materials in PDF format to: [email protected] Subject: Communication Studies Faculty Questions may be addressed to: Dr. Ignatius Fosu, Search Committee Chair [email protected] In accordance with applicable federal and state laws, such as Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act, and the Americans with Disabilities Act and ADA Amendments, the University does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, color, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, religion, or any other protected status under federal, state or local law applicable to the University, in its education policies, programs, and activities, in its admissions policies, in employment policies and practices, and all other areas of the University. As a faith-based institution, the University is exempted from certain laws and regulations concerning discrimination. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Communication/ Design/ Media Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Assistant Professor of Public Relations, Department of Communication and Media (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Posted - September 3, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Finance Grace College & Seminary Winona Lake, Indiana Posted - April 29, 2026 View Executive Assistant to the Provost WCIU Remote Posted - September 5, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of History LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 3, 2026 View Nursing - Assistant Professor Hope College Holland, Michigan Posted - September 4, 2026 View Religion Faculty Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Posted - September 4, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Azusa, California Florida Virginia Longview, Texas Birmingham, Alabama ORANGE CITY, Iowa Virginia Beach, Virginia St. Paul, Minnesota Oregon Iowa Alabama Portland, Oregon Houston, Texas West Palm Beach, Florida Texas Cedarville, Ohio California Minnesota Ohio Trending Companies Northwestern College Azusa Pacific University Samford University Palm Beach Atlantic University Houston Christian University LeTourneau University Cedarville University Regent University Trending Categories Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Engineering Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
