    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-professor-english-department-9-mo-tt-birmingham-alabama-12610": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, English Department (9 Mo, TT)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, English Department (9 Mo, TT) in Birmingham, Alabama | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant Professor, English Department (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Share Save Job Apply for This Job ASSISTANT PROFESSOR, ENGLISH DEPARTMENT (9-month, Tenure-Track Appointment) September 2, 2026 Samford University’s Howard College of Arts and Sciences invites individuals interested in serving in a Christian university environment to submit applications for a position as Assistant Professor of English, beginning August 2027. We seek a writer of fiction and/or nonfiction with secondary expertise in digital literacies, technologies of writing and research, and/or multimodal composition. This tenure-track position carries a twenty-four (24) credit hour teaching load per academic year, as well as expectations for active research and service. Teaching will include advanced and introductory courses for the Department and first-year writing courses for the General Education program. A robust and realistic scholarly agenda is expected, as is service to department, college, university, and community initiatives. Qualified candidates must hold an M FA in creative writing and/or a PhD or ABD, near completion, in English ; have a publication record as a writer of fiction or nonfiction; and be prepared to equip students to navigate the current digital landscape and utilize emerging technologies and AI. Applicants with secondary expertise in digital studies, digital literacies, and/or digital media are encouraged to apply. Applicants with training and experience teaching first-year writing are also encouraged to apply. Successful candidates will be committed to excellent teaching, student development and mentorship, and collegial collaboration. ABD candidates will be hired at the rank of Instructor, with a commensurate salary, until Ph.D. is completed. English studies has been a central focus of Samford University since the university’s founding in 1841, when the original institution was called the Howard College of English and Classical Studies. Fourteen faculty members serve approximately sixty majors in a traditional BA program of writing and literary study, in optional concentrations in Writing and Film, and minors in English, Film and Video Studies, and Writing. The department supports a master’s degree program in Samford’s Orlean Beeson School of Education and cooperates with Samford University’s 3-3 program in the Cumberland School of Law. For more information, see Samford’s English Department here . Located in the Homewood suburb of Birmingham, Alabama, Samford ( samford.edu ) is a leading Christian university offering undergraduate programs grounded in the liberal arts with an array of nationally recognized graduate and professional schools. Founded in 1841, Samford enrolls 6,324 students from 44 states, Puerto Rico and 16 countries in its 10 academic schools with 450 full-time faculty. Samford is ranked #3 in the nation for career preparation and #8 in the nation for student learning opportunities as listed in The Wall Street Journal (2026). The University is dedicated to the promotion of rigorous academic inquiry in a Christian setting. The University seeks and prefers employee applicants of the Christian faith and offers competitive salaries with a generous benefits package. Review of applications will begin November 15, 2026, and applications will be accepted until January 15, 2027. Please submit the following documents: 1) an application letter that includes statement of teaching philosophy and experience and a description of research interests and activities, 2) a curriculum vitae with contact information for three references, 3) an application for faculty position, and 4) the faculty applicant Christian mission statement. (The application and the statement are available at the links below.) Salary is dependent upon qualifications and experience. The successful candidate must pass a background check. Applicants must be authorized to work in the United States, as Samford will not sponsor any employment visa for this position. “Application for Faculty Position” can be found at: https://www.samford.edu/departments/files/Human_Resources/application-for-faculty-employment.pdf “Faculty Applicant Christian Mission Statement” can be found at: https://www.samford.edu/departments/files/academic-affairs/Faculty-Applicant-Christian-Mission-Statement.docx Please submit all materials in PDF format to: [email protected] Subject : Asst. Prof., English Questions may be addressed to the search committee chair, Dr. Brad Busbee ( [email protected] ). In accordance with applicable federal and state laws, such as Titles VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, the Age Discrimination in Employment Act, and the Americans with Disabilities Act and ADA Amendments, the University does not unlawfully discriminate on the basis of sex, gender, race, color, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, religion, or any other protected status under federal, state or local law applicable to the University, in its education policies, programs, and activities, in its admissions policies, in employment policies and practices, and all other areas of the University. As a faith-based institution, the University is exempted from certain laws and regulations concerning discrimination. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Tenure-track, Open-rank English Faculty Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Posted - September 3, 2026 View Virginia and Tom Williams Endowed Chair of American Literature, Department of English, Associate Professor or Professor Baylor University Waco, Texas Posted - July 15, 2026 View Faculty, Clinical Psychology - College of Education and Behavioral Sciences Azusa Pacific University Azusa, California Posted - August 27, 2026 View Program Director, MS Occupational Therapy Columbia International University Columbia, South Carolina Posted - September 8, 2026 View Assistant Professor of Children and Family Ministry Moody Bible Institute Chicago, Illinois Posted - September 8, 2026 View Adjunct Faculty – College Math for Elementary Teaching Moody Bible Institute Chicago, Illinois Posted - September 8, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Minnesota Ohio Longview, Texas Virginia Beach, Virginia California ORANGE CITY, Iowa Portland, Oregon Virginia Texas Oregon West Palm Beach, Florida Houston, Texas St. Paul, Minnesota Florida Azusa, California Birmingham, Alabama Iowa Alabama Cedarville, Ohio Trending Companies Samford University LeTourneau University Northwestern College Azusa Pacific University Palm Beach Atlantic University Houston Christian University Regent University Cedarville University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Engineering Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Psychology Education Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Religion Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
    },
    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/tenure-track-open-rank-english-faculty-clinton-mississippi-12609": {
      "title": "Tenure-track, Open-rank English Faculty",
      "description": "Tenure-track, Open-rank English Faculty in Clinton, Mississippi | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Tenure-track, Open-rank English Faculty Mississippi Christian University Clinton, Mississippi Share Save Job Apply for This Job Job Summary The Department of English and World Languages at Mississippi Christian University invites applications for a tenure-track, open-rank English faculty position beginning Fall 2027. We welcome applicants with the ability to teach a variety of generalist literature and writing courses. We also encourage applications from candidates whose areas of specialization will expand the breadth and variety of courses offered. Candidates should demonstrate enthusiasm for teaching undergraduate and graduate English courses as well as a willingness to support the department’s emphasis on a systematic, methods-driven approach to textual analysis. The ideal candidate will join a supportive and collaborative department dedicated to the needs of students, the mission of the department, and the mission of the university. Job Duties Teach four courses per semester, a combination of core curriculum and upper level courses Support, mentor, and advise students Contribute to ongoing strategic planning for the future of the department within the School of Christian Studies, Humanities and the Arts Keep a minimum of ten in-person office hours per week during each semester Serve on departmental and university committees Support Mississippi Christian University’s mission Minimum Qualifications Applicants must have a terminal degree in English or closely related field in hand before the start date of the appointment. To be considered, applicants must complete the Mississippi Christian University employment application and submit a letter of application, CV, and statement of teaching philosophy to [email protected] or Dr. David Miller, English Professor Search Committee, Box 4022, Mississippi Christian University, Clinton, MS  39058. Review of applications will begin on 12 November 2026. Transcripts and letters of recommendation will be requested after initial screenings. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to interview in early 2027. About the Department The Department of English and World Languages offers courses in literature, language, linguistics, cultural studies, textual analysis, qualitative research, English secondary education, and philosophy. Courses emphasize the exploration and production of a variety of texts in various modes with careful attention to replicable methodologies. The department also supports several minors: English studies for non-majors, applied humanities, African American studies, and philosophy. About the University Mississippi Christian University, with more than 80 undergraduate majors and 50 graduate areas of study, values its reputation for academic excellence and its commitment to the integration of faith and learning. Mississippi Christian University is a private comprehensive institution affiliated with the Mississippi Baptist Convention; it actively seeks faculty and staff who are committed Christians and whose Christian principles are exemplified in daily living. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - English Literature and Composition Education: Doctorate Degree Experience: Entry Level Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs ECE Program Director/Faculty (Early Childhood Education, Early Literacy, Early Math), Teacher Education Azusa Pacific University Azusa, California Posted - August 27, 2026 View Assistant Professor, English Department (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Posted - September 3, 2026 View Virginia and Tom Williams Endowed Chair of American Literature, Department of English, Associate Professor or Professor Baylor University Waco, Texas Posted - July 15, 2026 View Faculty, Clinical Psychology - College of Education and Behavioral Sciences Azusa Pacific University Azusa, California Posted - August 27, 2026 View Executive Assistant to the Provost WCIU Remote Posted - September 5, 2026 View Adjunct Faculty – College Math for Elementary Teaching Moody Bible Institute Chicago, Illinois Posted - September 8, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations ORANGE CITY, Iowa Longview, Texas Birmingham, Alabama Cedarville, Ohio Portland, Oregon Virginia Beach, Virginia Houston, Texas California Ohio Florida Alabama St. Paul, Minnesota Oregon West Palm Beach, Florida Virginia Iowa Azusa, California Minnesota Texas Trending Companies Northwestern College Regent University Houston Christian University Samford University Palm Beach Atlantic University Cedarville University Azusa Pacific University LeTourneau University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Health Professions Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Education Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
    },
    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-associate-or-full-professor-of-language-and-literacy-education-wenham-massachusetts-12608": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Language and Literacy Education",
      "description": "Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Language and Literacy Education in Wenham, Massachusetts | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor of Language and Literacy Education Gordon College Wenham, Massachusetts Share Save Job Apply for This Job The Herschend School of Education at Gordon College invites applications for a full time tenure track faculty position at the rank of assistant, associate, or full professor to teach in an Ed.D. program in the Science of Learning with emphasis on Language and Literacy Education. This is a primarily online program with an annual one week residential summer institute. Position to begin May or August 2027. Rank will be commensurate with experience. Gordon College is a Christian liberal arts college located in Massachusetts on Boston’s North Shore, a beautiful coastal area with easy access to Boston. This Ed.D. builds on the Herschend School’s thirty year history of rigorous graduate education programs grounded in evidence-based practices to equip all children to learn to read proficiently. Our graduate reading specialist program has the distinction of the “accreditation plus” rating by the International Dyslexia Association. We seek faculty excited to build on this legacy in a CPED-aligned doctoral program aiming to graduate scholar-practitioners ready to serve as the next generation of leaders, changeagents, problem solvers, and advocates within K-12 education, speech-language pathology clinical practice, education policy, and educator/SLP preparation. Responsibilities: • Teach online graduate courses and participate in annual residential summer institute; Depending on expertise, possible option to also teach in person undergraduate courses. • Advise students, supporting the full student experience, including timely degree completion; • Participate in and chair dissertation committees; • Serve on the admissions committee, collaborating to screen applicants and select new cohort members; • Engage in research and scholarly activities, including seeking grant funding and fostering external partnerships; • Engage in purposeful service to the institution and the profession. Qualifications of the Ideal Candidate: • A commitment to the Christian mission of the college; • Earned doctorate in education, speech-language pathology, cognitive psychology, or a closely related field; • Expertise in the science of learning, language and literacy education, instructional leadership, and/or research methods; • Commitment to evidence-based practices to equitably support all learners, including culturally and linguistically sustaining practices; • Three or more years of experience with K-12 teaching/tutoring, SLP clinical practice, or applied research; • Evidence of effective teaching, with preference for experience teaching in online settings; • Demonstrated leadership in education or clinical settings; • Active research program with potential for student collaboration; • Passion for mentoring aspiring literacy leaders; • Strong interpersonal skills with ability to communicate and collaborate with faculty, staff, and students. Interested Applicants Must Submit: • Cover letter that addresses the applicant’s fit with the Christian mission of Gordon College and a rationale for interest in this specific position; • CV that includes the names and contact information for 3 references; • A sample of academic writing. Anticipated Salary Range: $64,733 - $97,300 commensurate with experience. TO APPLY: https://www.gordon.edu/offices-services/human-resources/jobs/open-facultypositions#full-time Visit https://www.gordon.edu/offices-services/human-resources/for-prospective-employees for more information on Gordon College. Our review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Gordon College is an equal opportunity employer. Qualified applicants for employment will receive consideration without discrimination on the basis of race, color, gender, age, national origin, or disability. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Education Salary: $64,733 - $97,300 Per Year Education: Doctorate Degree Experience: 10 - 20 years Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Assistant Professor, English Department (9 Mo, TT) Samford University Birmingham, Alabama Posted - September 3, 2026 View Executive Assistant to the Provost WCIU Remote Posted - September 5, 2026 View Program Director, MS Occupational Therapy Columbia International University Columbia, South Carolina Posted - September 8, 2026 View Assistant or Associate Professor of Education Spring Arbor University Spring Arbor, Michigan Posted - September 8, 2026 View Religion Faculty Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Posted - September 4, 2026 View Nursing - Assistant Professor Hope College Holland, Michigan Posted - September 4, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Houston, Texas West Palm Beach, Florida Longview, Texas Oregon Virginia Beach, Virginia Iowa Cedarville, Ohio Portland, Oregon Azusa, California St. Paul, Minnesota California Ohio Florida ORANGE CITY, Iowa Alabama Texas Birmingham, Alabama Minnesota Virginia Trending Companies Palm Beach Atlantic University Samford University Houston Christian University Regent University LeTourneau University Azusa Pacific University Northwestern College Cedarville University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Engineering Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Health Professions Education Faculty Careers - Religion Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
