    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/biology-faculty-orange-city-iowa-12607": {
      "title": "Biology Faculty",
      "description": "Biology Faculty in ORANGE CITY, Iowa | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Biology Faculty Northwestern College ORANGE CITY, Iowa Share Save Job Apply for This Job Northwestern College seeks to fill a full-time tenure-track assistant professor position in the department of biology beginning in August of 2027. Ideal candidates will be well rounded in biology and have the ability to teach a broad range of biological courses. The successful candidate will teach introductory anatomy and physiology and upper-level courses in microbiology, cell biology, and/or molecular genetics, depending on the expertise of the candidate. There will also be possible opportunities to teach in areas of specialization within an undergraduate curriculum. The teaching load for this position is 24 credit hours per academic year. The successful candidate will also be responsible for scholarship and service, including recruiting and advising biology students. Northwestern enjoys a strong reputation in the sciences based on the career accomplishments of our faculty and graduates, and on the college’s commitment to courageous and confident inquiry, exploration and discovery of God’s truth as it is revealed through the natural world. Our $24.5 million DeWitt Family Science Center is testimony to our investment in the sciences. Required Qualifications: Applicants should have a Ph.D. in biology or a closely related field to be considered for a tenure track position (ABD will also be considered). Candidates should demonstrate evidence for excellent classroom teaching and engagement in scholarship. Preferred Qualifications: Preferred candidates will have demonstrated experience in higher education and research interests conducive to student involvement. Northwestern College seeks candidates with an authentic Christian faith who will embrace and live out our mission & values , including our Reformed, evangelical and ecumenical identity as stated in our Christian Identity Statement, Mission Statement, Vision for Learning and Vision for Diversity. We view these statements as complementary and draw from each in fulfilling our mission. We seek faculty invested in teaching, a program of scholarly activity, and the mission of excellence in the liberal arts, as a vital expression of commitment to Christ’s redemptive work in the world. Apply online and send a letter of interest in which you (1) describe your teaching experience and (2) scholarly trajectory; and (3) discuss how the following statements would inform and shape your teaching and scholarship: our Statement of Christian Identity , Vision for Learning and Vision for Diversity . Include a current curriculum vitae/resume and send to [email protected] . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Biology/ Life Sciences Education: Doctorate Degree Experience: Less than 2 years Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Visiting Faculty - Biology Northwestern College ORANGE CITY, Iowa Posted - August 25, 2026 View Program Director, MS Occupational Therapy Columbia International University Columbia, South Carolina Posted - September 8, 2026 View Assistant or Associate Professor of Education Spring Arbor University Spring Arbor, Michigan Posted - September 8, 2026 View Religion Faculty Calvin University Grand Rapids, Michigan Posted - September 4, 2026 View Executive Assistant to the Provost WCIU Remote Posted - September 5, 2026 View Nursing - Assistant Professor Hope College Holland, Michigan Posted - September 4, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations Virginia Houston, Texas Virginia Beach, Virginia West Palm Beach, Florida Portland, Oregon Ohio Texas Minnesota Oregon Birmingham, Alabama Cedarville, Ohio ORANGE CITY, Iowa Iowa Florida St. Paul, Minnesota Longview, Texas Alabama Azusa, California California Trending Companies Azusa Pacific University Regent University Samford University Houston Christian University Northwestern College LeTourneau University Cedarville University Palm Beach Atlantic University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Health Professions Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Education Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
