    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/faculty-in-residence-criminal-justice-legal-studies-saint-bonifacius-minnesota-12598": {
      "title": "Faculty in Residence",
      "description": "Faculty in Residence - Criminal Justice & Legal Studies in Saint Bonifacius, Minnesota | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Faculty in Residence - Criminal Justice & Legal Studies Crown College Saint Bonifacius, Minnesota Share Save Job Apply for This Job Location 8700 College View Drive, Saint Bonifacius, MN, 55375, United States Required Degree Masters Manage Others No Contact information Name : Dr. Kelli Corti Email [email protected] Description EFFECTIVE DATE: July 1, 2026 FLSA STATUS: Exempt HOURS WORKED: 15-20 hours weekly during regular academic terms This is a part-time faculty position to teach undergraduate criminal justice courses on campus within the School of Liberal Arts and Education. Teaching responsibilities are assigned by the Chair of the Department of Humanities and Social Science. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: This position reports to the Chair of the Department of Humanities and Social Science , the Dean of the School of Liberal Arts and Education , and the Vice President of Academic Affairs . SUPERVISORY FUNCTIONS: None. EQUIPMENT/JOB LOCATION: Works from an office at Crown College.  Equipment used includes, but is not limited to, personal computer and required programs, printer, fax machine, calculator, copy machines, and other equipment as the position requires. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE JOB: · Teach two courses per normal academic term related to criminal justice. Courses may include Criminal Procedure, Criminal Statues & Enforcement, and Criminal Investigations. · Hold an average of at least 6 office hours per week during the normal academic terms. Participate in department and faculty meetings as available Academic advising for Criminal Justice and Legal Studies students as needed REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, AND ABILITIES: · Demonstrated experience and expertise in teaching criminal justice courses at the college level · Strong interpersonal skills and positive energy regarding professional education · Established ability to work effectively as a team member · Demonstrate excellence in spoken, written and electronic communication skills · Ability to integrate collegiate teaching and the Christian faith · Experience evaluating students’ work and reporting results promptly · Hands-on experience in the criminal justice or legal field through previous work and/or consulting experience · Ability and willingness to stay abreast of the ever-changing criminal justice environment in order to maintain relevancy in teaching criminal justice courses to college-level students · Skill to organize and manage multiple tasks simultaneously · Agreement and personal alignment with the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant PHYSICAL DEMANDS: The physical demands described herein are representative of those required of an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Stamina to stand for extended periods of time in classroom Hand and arm (or equivalent) dexterity adequate to allow for safe use of equipment and extensive use of a keyboard for data entry Vocal strength to speak clearly in classroom for extended periods of time Vision adequate for frequent viewing of computer screens and safe use and supervision of equipment and materials Body strength to frequently lift and/or move up to twenty-five (25) pounds MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: · Master’s level degree in criminal justice or a related field, or Bachelor degree in relevant criminal justice-related field AND a minimum of 10 years’ direct experience in a relevant criminal justice-related field · Demonstrated teaching effectiveness · Work experience in criminal justice, law enforcement, law, corrections, or a related field · Experience using computer technology in the teaching/learning process PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS (in addition to the above minimum qualifications): · A PhD or terminal degree in a related field · 5+ years of full-time teaching experience, especially in Christian higher education · Familiarity and/or experience with standards and assessments · Experience with academic advising/mentoring NON-DISCRIMINATION POLICY: Crown College will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, or status with regard to public assistance. Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Criminal Justice Salary: $15,000 - $25,000 Per Year Education: Bachelor's Degree Experience: 2 - 5 years Position Type: Part Time Related Jobs Vice President Academic and Dean Booth University College Winnipeg, Manitoba, Canada Posted - August 12, 2026 View Assistant Professor of Children and Family Ministry Moody Bible Institute Chicago, Illinois Posted - September 8, 2026 View Adjunct Faculty – College Math for Elementary Teaching Moody Bible Institute Chicago, Illinois Posted - September 8, 2026 View Program Director, MS Occupational Therapy Columbia International University Columbia, South Carolina Posted - September 8, 2026 View Executive Assistant to the Provost WCIU Remote Posted - September 5, 2026 View Assistant or Associate Professor of Education Spring Arbor University Spring Arbor, Michigan Posted - September 8, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Nursing Assistant Professor Associate Professor of Finance Trending Locations Florida Minnesota Virginia Beach, Virginia Azusa, California Longview, Texas West Palm Beach, Florida Houston, Texas Texas Iowa Virginia Oregon St. Paul, Minnesota Birmingham, Alabama Ohio Alabama California ORANGE CITY, Iowa Cedarville, Ohio Portland, Oregon Trending Companies Palm Beach Atlantic University Regent University Samford University Houston Christian University Northwestern College Cedarville University Azusa Pacific University LeTourneau University Trending Categories Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Faculty Careers - Religion Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
