    "https://careers.cccu.org/job/assistant-associate-professor-of-nursing-saint-bonifacius-minnesota-12597": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing in Saint Bonifacius, Minnesota | Council for Christian Colleges and Universities Home Search Directory Contact Us Career Resources Career Advice Interview Coach Offer Analyzer Pricing Register Job Seekers Employers Sign In Post a Job Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing Crown College Saint Bonifacius, Minnesota Share Save Job Apply for This Job Description This is a full time, tenure-track faculty position within the School of Health and Science teaching undergraduate nursing courses on campus and supervising nursing students in clinical settings. Teaching responsibilities are assigned by the Chair of the Department of Nursing. SUPERVISION RECEIVED This position reports to the Chair of the Department of Nursing, the Dean of the School of Health and Science, and the Vice President of Academic Affairs . SUPERVISORY FUNCTIONS Adjunct and clinical faculty who may be assigned within a course. EQUIPMENT/JOB LOCATION Works from an office at Crown College. Regular attendance on campus to complete job duties is required. Equipment used includes, but is not limited to, personal computer and related software, printer, copy machines, Nursing Simulation Lab equipment and tools related to undergraduate teaching and research. Travel to clinical sites will also be required. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS OF THE JOB · Teach courses within the prescribed nursing curriculum utilizing a variety of teaching methodologies to engage students in the learning process. A normal teaching load is 24 credits each year. · Teaching in simulation lab · Facilitate student development of knowledge, skills, and demeanor required for professional practice as a nurse. · Supervise students in clinical settings. · Advise students in the Department of Nursing. · Stay abreast of scholarly developments in specific and relevant fields as well as current teaching methodologies, curriculum development, and assessment. · Contribute to the field of nursing and/or the profession of college-level teaching. · Participate in measures to maintain compliance with Minnesota State Board of Nursing and Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education. · Support the mission, goals and objectives of Crown College. · Engage in general faculty responsibilities that include: o Participation in department and faculty meetings, o Care of students, o Crown College committee assignments, and o At least 10 hours of scheduled office hours on campus per week to be available to students. REQUIRED KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES · Demonstrated experience and expertise teaching nursing courses at the college level. · Demonstrated experience in simulation labs. · Strong interpersonal skills and an enthusiasm for working with students pursuing higher education. · Established ability to work effectively as a team member. · Demonstrate excellence and professionalism in spoken, written and electronic communication skills when with prospective and current students, faculty, and staff, as well as clinical agency representatives. · Ability to integrate collegiate teaching and the Christian faith. · Experience evaluating students’ work and reporting results promptly. · Agreement and personal alignment with the Crown College Statement of Faith and Community Covenant. · Must be a committed Christian who is active in a local church PHYSICAL DEMANDS The physical demands described herein are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Stamina to stand for extended periods of time (in the classroom, in the simulation lab, and in clinical settings). Mobility to allow for safe movement within lab and clinical environments. Hand and arm (or equivalent) dexterity adequate to allow for patient care, safe use of equipment, and extensive use of a keyboard for data entry. Vocal strength to speak clearly in a classroom and lab for extended periods of time. Vision adequate for frequent viewing of computer screens and safe use and supervision of equipment and materials. Body strength to frequently lift and/ or move up to ten (10) pounds. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS · Master of Science in Nursing or equivalent degree · Relevant experience as a nurse · Current unencumbered RN License · Demonstrated teaching effectiveness · Current American Heart Association Healthcare Provider BLS Certification (or equivalent). · Experience using computer technology in the teaching/learning process PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS (in addition to the above minimum qualifications) · Earned DNP, PhD in Nursing or other equivalent terminal degree. · Experience as a nurse in OB, acute medical/surgical, ICU, Emergency, or related area. · Unencumbered RN Licensure in Minnesota · 3+ years of full-time teaching experience, especially in Christian higher education · Familiarity and/or experience with standards and assessments, especially related to the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education and the Minnesota Board of Nursing · Experience with advising BENEFITS Crown College offers a generous and comprehensive benefits package for full-time staff and faculty, designed to support the health, well-being, and financial future of our employees. Benefits include medical coverage through Medica, dental coverage through Delta Dental, and vision coverage through EyeMed. Employees also receive employer-paid basic life insurance equal to one times their annual salary, subject to policy limits, with optional voluntary benefits including supplemental life insurance, hospital indemnity, critical illness, and short-term disability coverage. A Health Savings Account (HSA) is available for employees enrolled in the high-deductible health plan. In addition to competitive benefits, Crown offers generous paid vacation, sick leave, and holiday pay, along with a 403(b) retirement plan that includes an employer contribution. ENVIRONMENT AND LOCATION Employees enjoy working on our beautiful lakeside campus, which features an on-campus fitness center, scenic walking paths leading to Parley Lake and convenient access to our on-campus Frisbie Golf Course. These amenities provide excellent opportunities to stay active, recharge, and enjoy the natural beauty of the campus throughout the year. Non-Discrimination Policy Crown College will not discriminate against or harass any employee or applicant for employment because of race, color, national origin, sex, disability, age, or status regarding public assistance. (The examples given above are intended only as illustrations of various types of work performed and are not necessarily all-inclusive.  This position description is subject to change as the needs of the employer and requirements of the position change.  Crown College reserves the right to change and/or eliminate all job duties as determined necessary.) Job Information Job Category: Faculty Careers - Health Professions Salary: $62,000 - $73,000 Per Year Education: Master's Degree Experience: 2 - 5 years Position Type: Full Time Related Jobs Director, The Center for Academic MInistry LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - August 21, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing, Undergraduate Program - Community Nursing Palm Beach Atlantic University West Palm Beach, Florida Posted - August 21, 2026 View Nursing - Assistant Professor Hope College Holland, Michigan Posted - September 4, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of History LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - September 3, 2026 View Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing, Undergraduate Program - Pediatrics Palm Beach Atlantic University West Palm Beach, Florida Posted - August 21, 2026 View Assistant or Associate Professor of Accounting LeTourneau University Longview, Texas Posted - August 21, 2026 View Show More Jobs Trending Job Titles Associate Professor of Finance Nursing Assistant Professor Trending Locations Longview, Texas Portland, Oregon Virginia Cedarville, Ohio Oregon Iowa Birmingham, Alabama Alabama Minnesota Texas California Azusa, California St. Paul, Minnesota Ohio Florida Houston, Texas Virginia Beach, Virginia West Palm Beach, Florida ORANGE CITY, Iowa Trending Companies Azusa Pacific University Samford University LeTourneau University Houston Christian University Northwestern College Palm Beach Atlantic University Regent University Cedarville University Trending Categories Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Religion Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Education Faculty Careers - Psychology Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Apply for this job Find Jobs By Category Education Faculty Careers - Health Professions Faculty Careers - Biology/Life Sciences Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Other Faculty Careers - Psychology Higher Ed Administrative Careers - Development/Fundraising Faculty Careers - Engineering Faculty Careers - Communication/Design/Media Faculty Careers - Religion Powered by Web Scribble Solutions , Inc. About Our Work & Mission Our Institutions Leadership Contact Us Join Us Advertise Donate Employment Membership Sponsorship Follow Us Council for Christian Colleges & Universities 20 M Street SE, Suite 350 , Washington, D.C. 20003 202.546.8713"
